{Time limit 48 moves in 2hrs then 24 moves per hr} 1. c4 {I knew he would be
expecting a KS opening.} Nf6 2. g3 g6 3. Bg2 Bg7 4. Nc3 c6 5. e4 e5 6. Nge2 O-O
7. O-O d6 {Black decides to try and force ...d5} 8. h3 Be6 {Doesn't turn out
too well.} 9. b3 Qd7 {[23'] Not a very good idea. The Queen is badly placed
here. I was concerned about ...d5} 10. Kh2 {[6']} Na6 11. d4 {Highlighting his
problems by threatening to win the Bishop.} exd4 12. Nxd4 Nc5 13. Ba3 Rad8 14.
Rc1 ({I considered} 14. e5 dxe5 15. Bxc5 exd4 16. Bxf8 Kxf8 {but Black gets a
lot of play.}) 14... Rfe8 15. f4 {Threatening to win his Bishop again.} Qc7 16.
Rc2 Bc8 {[53']} 17. Re1 {[30']} Qd7 {Threatening a mass exchange on e4,
followed by .....Qxh3+} 18. Rce2 Re7 $2 {Intending to double on the e-file but
my reply wins a Pawn.} 19. e5 Nh5 $2 (19... Ne8 $142) 20. exd6 Rxe2 21. Ndxe2
Ne6 (21... b6 $142) 22. c5 b6 23. b4 Re8 24. Qd2 ({If} 24. b5 Bb7) 24... bxc5
25. bxc5 Ba6 {Black plays rather passively leaving his Queen in a blockading
role.} 26. Bf3 Nf6 27. g4 Rc8 ({Passive again. Why not} 27... Rb8) 28. g5 Ne8
29. Bg4 f5 30. Bf3 N8c7 31. Kg3 Nb5 {Exchanges favour White.} 32. Nxb5 Bxb5 33.
Nc3 Ba6 34. Bd1 Re8 {He was getting very short of time now.} 35. Bb3 Bc8 36.
Bb2 Kf8 37. Na4 Bxb2 38. Qxb2 Qg7 39. Qd2 ({I briefly considered} 39. Qg2) ({
and} 39. Re5) 39... Qd4 {Probably better to keep Queens on.} 40. Qxd4 Nxd4 41.
Rxe8+ Kxe8 42. Kf2 {Hoping that he'd exchange again.} Nxb3 $2 {Suicide, short
of time he grabs the Bishop to leave himself with a hopeless endgame. Better...
...} (42... Be6 43. Bxe6 {forced} Nxe6 {and White has a hard time even if the
win is possible.}) 43. axb3 Be6 44. b4 Kd7 45. Ke3 Bb3 46. Nc3 Ke6 47. Kd4 {
I didn't fancy 47.b5 due to his passed a-Pawn.} a6 {This makes it marginally
easier for White to win.} 48. Kd3 Kd7 {The game was adjourned.} 49. Kd2 {
[Sealed move] The game resumed 10/10/76. White has an easy win. Black's Bishop
may as well not be on the board and his King tied to my d-Pawn. White can win
the h-Pawn with the Knight.} Ke6 50. Nd1 Bd5 51. Ne3 Be4 52. Kc3 Bf3 53. Kd4
Bd5 54. Nc4 Bg2 55. h4 Bf3 56. Nb6 Bh5 57. Nc8 Bf3 58. Ne7 Bd5 59. Ng8 Bg2 60.
Nf6 Bf3 61. Nxh7 Bh5 62. Nf8+ Kf7 63. Nd7 {An enjoyable game.} 1-0

