{Time limit 36 moves in 1hr 30'} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nd2 Nf6 4. e5 Nfd7 5. f4
c5 6. c3 Nc6 7. Ngf3 Qb6 8. Nb3 Na5 $2 {The rot sets in. As usual I was on a
hiding to nothing and "had to win" so my play becomes artificial. I realised
my mistake immediately.} 9. Be3 $2 (9. dxc5 $1 {and I can't recapture.}) 9...
Nc4 10. Bxc4 dxc4 11. dxc5 Nxc5 $2 (11... Qa6 $142 {as I originally intended.})
12. Nxc5 Bxc5 13. Bxc5 Qxc5 14. Qd4 Qxd4 15. Nxd4 {Now White has slightly the
better of it but I felt that I had to win and continued to play artificially.}
a6 16. O-O g6 $2 (16... Bd7 {and 17...0-0-0 is best.}) 17. Rfd1 b6 $2 {My
attempts to activate the bishop simply lose the d-file.} 18. Nc2 Bb7 19. Rd6 {
[35']} Be4 {[58']} 20. Ne3 b5 21. Rad1 h5 {To prevent 22 Ng4.} (21... Bd3 $142)
22. R1d4 Bb1 {[1hr 10'] I was taking ages trying to find a winning line.} 23.
a3 {Good enough but 23.a4 may be better.} (23. a4) 23... O-O 24. Nd1 Kg7 25.
Nf2 {[51']} Rfb8 $2 {Rushing now.} 26. Rd7 a5 {[1hr 24'] The remainder
happened very quickly.} 27. Nh3 b4 28. Ng5 bxa3 29. Rxf7+ Kg8 30. Rdd7 Bf5 31.
Nh7 g5 32. Nf6+ Kh8 33. Rh7+ {Terrible. I considered giving up playing after
this. I may restrict myself to games where a draw is acceptable as a result.}
1-0

