{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. e4 {[4']} e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Bxc6
dxc6 5. O-O Bg4 6. h3 Bxf3 7. Qxf3 {[6']} Qf6 {[0']} 8. Qg3 Bc5 {[3'] I had
expected this opening and had been through a number of lines this evening
including my game v John Toothill (9/11/77) he had played 8...Bc5 but I had a
note saying possibly ...Bd6 is probably better.} (8... Bd6 {how about} 9. b4 {
now?}) 9. d3 {[17']} h6 {[5']} ({John had played} 9... Ne7 {but I was unhappy
about} 10. Bg5 {(why hadn't I played that?) However, maybe} Qg6 {is O.K. as}
11. Qxe5 Bd6 12. Qa5 b6 {wins the Bishop.}) 10. Be3 {[21']} Bxe3 {[11'] John
had retreated ...Bd6. I felt that would stamp my 8th move as wrong.} 11. fxe3
Qg5 12. Qe1 {[27'] Best I think.} Ne7 {[14']} 13. Nd2 {[27']} O-O $2 {
Carelessness, probably playing too quickly} 14. Nf3 Qf6 ({If} 14... Qh5 15. Qb4
) 15. h4 $2 ({Much to my surprise. I was expecting} 15. Qa5 {which wins at
least a pawn.}) 15... Qd6 16. Rd1 {[38']} c5 {[25']} ({I considered} 16... f5)
17. g4 {[42']} b6 {[30'] Don't panic; solidify on the QS.} 18. b3 Nc6 19. Rd2
a5 20. Qg3 {[53']} ({I felt that} 20. a4 {denying me any QS play was more
correct.}) 20... a4 {[35']} 21. Rdf2 axb3 22. axb3 {[56']} Qe7 {[46'] Holding
steady} 23. g5 h5 24. Nd2 g6 {This surprised him he hadn't seen my 25th move.}
25. Rf6 Nb8 26. R1f2 {[1hr 10']} Nd7 27. Rc6 Nb8 28. Rcf6 Nd7 {[59'] He was
just gaining a bit of time on the clock.} 29. R6f3 Ra2 30. Nf1 Qe6 {[64'] Here
I offered a draw which he accepted. Ian's last two games were wins against
Kotov! in the match which he won 2-1 last weekend. Ian had a FIDE rating of
2220 and a CX title.} 1/2-1/2

