{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15' then 6 moves per 15'} 1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4
cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 6. Be2 Be7 7. O-O O-O 8. Kh1 {I decided to play it
very solidly.} a6 9. a4 {[4']} Nc6 {[10']} 10. f4 e5 11. Nxc6 {[9']} bxc6 12.
fxe5 {I felt that his disconnected Pawns might compensate for the half open
b-file.} dxe5 13. Be3 Rb8 {Rather awkward for White.} 14. Rb1 {[19'] Best I
think.} (14. b3 {leaves the knight weak so} Bb4 {threatens to take off the
Knight, and win the e-Pawn.}) 14... Qa5 {[34']} 15. Bd3 {[24'] I decided to
close the d-file and support the e-pawn.} ({If} 15. Qe1 {then} Bb4 {is a
nuisance.}) 15... Be6 {[36']} 16. Qe1 {With thoughts of some KS play. Also Nd5
is good in some lines.} Kh8 17. Bg5 {Discouraging 17.......Bb4} Ng8 18. Bxe7
Nxe7 19. b3 Rfd8 {He said that he overlooked my reply.} 20. b4 $1 {Seizing the
initiative. I could have played this last move.} Qb6 {[56']} 21. a5 {[49']} Qd4
{Black prefers to keep some active chances.} ({Maybe} 21... Qa7 {is better but
White is well on top with} 22. Na4) 22. Bxa6 ({If} 22. Na4 Ba2) 22... Ng6 ({If
} 22... Rxb4 23. Rd1 {wins.}) 23. Na4 {[57']} Bc4 $2 {[69'] Getting short of
time he miscalculates.} 24. c3 Qd3 {Threatening 25.......QxR+ However......}
25. Rf3 Qxb1 26. Qxb1 Bxa6 27. Nb2 Rd2 28. Kg1 Rbd8 29. g3 {[1hr 12' 30s]} Be2
30. Rxf7 Bg4 31. Qc1 {I felt that I just had to be careful now.} h5 32. Rf2 {
32......Rd1+ would leave him unable to stop the a-Pawn.} R2d6 33. h4 Nf8 34.
Kh2 Nh7 35. Nc4 {Having tidied up at the back I can start going forward.} Rd1
36. Qb2 Re1 37. Nxe5 {Preventing 37......R8d1 in view of 38.Ng6+ and 39.Qb3+}
Be6 (37... Rdd1 38. Ng6+ Kg8 39. Qb3+) 38. Rd2 {Contesting the d-file as he
can't transfer the Rook to f8.} Re8 39. Nxc6 {I now have so many Pawns that I
may be able to give up Queen for Rook if it gets too hot.} Nf6 40. Rd8 Ng4+ 41.
Kg2 Rxd8 42. Nxd8 Bc4 ({naturally not} 42... Ne3+ 43. Kf2 Nd1+ {is good for
White with his bishop en prise. We now had to adjourn}) (42... Bc4 43. Qd2 {
The win for White is quite clear. Black has 2 main lines.} Re2+ (43... Rxe4 {
if now} 44. Kf3 {then} (44. Qd6 $1 {Threatening a6, and to win the Rook by Qf8+
} Nf6 (44... Re2+ 45. Kf3 Re3+ (45... Ne5+ 46. Kf4 Nd3+ 47. Kf5 Rf2+ 48. Ke4 {
etc.}) (45... Nh2+ 46. Kf4 Rf2+ 47. Ke4 Re2+ 48. Kd4 $1 Rd2+ 49. Kxc4 Rxd6 50.
Nf7+) (45... Rf2+ 46. Ke4 Re2+ 47. Kd4 {etc.}) 46. Kf4 $18) 45. a6 Bd5 46. Nf7+
Kh7 (46... Bxf7 47. Qf8+ Bg8 48. a7) (46... Kg8 47. Ng5 Rxb4+ 48. Qxd5+ Nxd5
49. cxb4 Nxb4 50. a7) 47. Ng5+) 44... Nf6 45. Z0 Bd5 {is very awkward.}) 44.
Qxe2 Bxe2 45. Nf7+ Kg8 46. Nd6 {threatening b5, a6 etc. e.g.} Ne3+ ({Fritz
gives} 46... Bd3 47. b5 Ne3+ 48. Kf3 Nc4 49. Nxc4 Bxc4 50. b6 Ba6 51. c4) 47.
Kf2 Nc4 48. e5 Bd3 49. Nxc4 Bxc4 50. Ke3 {etc.}) 43. Qd2 {[Sealed move] He
didn't want to see any of these variations; Three days later he phoned up to
resign! A good result. Sources: RA Collins; ID Wells scorebook (which lacks
the sealed move)} 1-0

