1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 e6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 6. Be2 Be7 7. O-O O-O 8. f4
Nc6 9. Kh1 e5 10. Nb3 a5 11. a4 Nb4 12. Bf3 Be6 13. f5 Bc4 14. Re1 Qc7 15. Nd2
Rfd8 16. Nxc4 Qxc4 17. Qe2 Rac8 18. Bg5 h6 19. Bxf6 Bxf6 20. Rad1 Rc5 21. Qf2
Rc6 22. Re2 Qc5 23. g3 Bg5 24. Kg2 Qxf2+ 25. Kxf2 Rdc8 26. Kf1 Kf8 27. h4 Bd8
28. Nb5 Nxc2 29. Nxd6 Rb8 30. Nb5 Bb6 31. Rd7 Ne3+ 32. Kg1 Ke8 33. Rd3 Nxf5+
34. Kg2 Nd4 35. Nxd4 Bxd4 36. Red2 Rc1 37. Bd1 Rbc8 38. Bb3 Rg1+ 39. Kh3 Rf1 ({
Black could seal the win with} 39... h5) 40. Bd5 b6 41. h5 Rcc1 42. Kg4 Ke7 43.
Rf3 Rxf3 44. Kxf3 Kd6 45. Kg4 Rf1 46. Bc4 Re1 47. Re2 Rxe2 48. Bxe2 Bxb2 49.
Kf5 Kc5 50. Bb5 Kd4 51. Be8 b5 52. Bxb5 g6+ 53. hxg6 fxg6+ 54. Kxg6 Kxe4 55.
Kxh6 Kf5 56. Bd7+ {Black's c-file play seems to balance White's on the d-file.
18....h6 is bad because it means my B can't stay on the c1-h6 diagonal. The
exchange of Q's favours Black and the idea of B d8-b6-d4 gives him additional
advantage. Black could secure the win with 39....h5} 1/2-1/2

