{Time limit 30 moves in 1hr 15'} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Bxc6 dxc6 5.
O-O Bg4 6. h3 h5 7. d3 Bxf3 ({Normal is} 7... Qf6 {but I was completely out of
practice and couldn't remember much about it.}) 8. Qxf3 Qf6 $5 {Leads to a bad
game.} 9. Qxf6 Nxf6 10. Nd2 Bd6 {I wasn't happy about this.} 11. Nc4 Nd7 12. b3
f6 $5 13. Bb2 c5 {I was probably putting too many Pawns on Black squares.} 14.
Rae1 O-O 15. g3 Rae8 16. Kg2 g6 17. f4 b5 18. Ne3 c6 19. h4 Rf7 20. f5 {Help!}
g5 21. hxg5 fxg5 22. a4 Ra8 23. Ra1 Nf6 {n.b. Wells's own version of the score
ends here - 1-0} 24. Rh1 {[23']} Rff8 {[60']} 25. Nf1 c4 {[1hr 12']} 26. bxc4
bxc4 27. Nd2 cxd3 28. cxd3 Rab8 29. Nc4 Rfd8 {I lost on time. After this game
lack of time and enthusiasm caused me to give up playing chess, at least
temporarily. Sources: RA Collins; ID Wells scorebook} 1-0

